# Cloudflare Pages reads this from the deploy root. Anything in public/ is copied
# to dist/ verbatim by Astro, so this ships in the zip.
#
# Why this file exists: the outgoing WordPress site's sitemap contains exactly two
# indexed URLs, "/" and "/our-menu/" (verified 2026-07-24 against
# https://macalusositalianrestaurant.com/page-sitemap1.xml). "/our-menu/" is the menu,
# which is the single highest-intent page a restaurant has, and it is linked from the
# Google Business Profile and the social bios. Without this line it 404s the moment the
# nameservers flip and its accumulated ranking signal is thrown away instead of passed on.
#
# Note on fragments: the old page used #main-course, #brunch and #wine-cocktail. Fragments
# are never sent to the server, so they ride along to the new URL. "#brunch" happens to
# exist on the new menu page; the other two do not, so those visitors land at the top of
# the menu. That is acceptable. Do not try to redirect fragments here.

/our-menu     /menu/     301
/our-menu/    /menu/     301
